  "description_short": "Historic tea garden in Great Brak River serving homemade cakes, light meals, and traditional South African favorites.",
  "description_long": "Tucked away in the quiet Bergsig area of Great Brak River, Die Ou Pastorie Teetuin occupies a charming historic building that once served as the local parsonage. The garden setting creates a peaceful atmosphere perfect for a relaxed breakfast or leisurely lunch, with shaded outdoor seating under established trees.\n\nThe menu focuses on homemade goodness — freshly baked cakes, scones with jam and cream, and traditional South African light meals that draw locals and travelers alike. Their generous portions and warm service have earned them a loyal following over the years. The tea garden's unpretentious approach and home-style cooking make it a refreshing stop along the Garden Route.\n\nLocated just off the N2 between Mossel Bay and George, it's an easy detour for those exploring the area. The relaxed pace and genuinely friendly welcome make it feel like visiting a friend's home rather than just another roadside stop.",
